Phymosia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Malvaceae. It includes five species native to Mexico, Guatemala, El Salvador, Hispaniola, and the Bahamas.

Species
Five species are accepted.
Phymosia abutiloides {{small|(L.) Desv. ex Ham.}}
Phymosia anomala {{small|[[Paul Fryxell|Fryxell]]}}
Phymosia crenulata {{small|(Brandegee) Fryxell}}
Phymosia floribunda {{small|(Schltdl.) Fryxell}}
Phymosia pauciflora {{small|(Baker f.) Fryxell}}
Phymosia rosea {{small|(DC.) Kearney}} – El Salvador, Guatemala and Mexico
Phymosia rzedowskii {{small|Fryxell}}
Phymosia umbellata {{small|(Cav.) Kearney}} – Mexico
